⏺ GSD + Ralph-Loop Guide                                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                                  
  What is GSD?                                                                                                                                      
                                                                                                                                                    
  GSD (Get Shit Done) is a project management system built into your Claude Code setup. It turns big ideas into executable plans using a consistent 
  cycle: initialize → plan → execute → verify → repeat.                                                                                             
                                                                                                                                                    
  Rather than one massive conversation where Claude tries to build everything at once, GSD breaks work into phases, each phase into plans, each plan
   into tasks — and it uses specialized subagents for each step.
                                                                                                                                                    
  ---                                                                                                                                               
  The Core Loop                                
                                                                                                                                                    
  new-project → plan-phase → execute-phase → verify → repeat
                                                                                                                                                    
  Everything GSD creates lives in .planning/ in your project root. All decisions, research, plans, and progress are written to files — so nothing is
   lost between sessions.                                                                                                                           
                                                                                                                                                    
  ---                                          
  Starting a New Project                       
                        
  Step 1: (Brownfield only) Map the existing codebase
                                                                                                                                                    
  /gsd:map-codebase                                                                                                                                 
  Run this first if you have an existing codebase. It spawns 4 parallel agents to analyze your stack, architecture, conventions, tests,             
  integrations, and concerns. Creates .planning/codebase/ with 7 reference documents that every future agent reads.                                 
                                                                                                                                                    
  Skip this on a fresh project with no code yet.                                                                                                    
                                                                                                                                                    
  Step 2: Initialize the project               
                                                                                                                                                    
  /gsd:new-project                           
  This one command does everything:                                                                                                                 
  - Asks questions to understand what you're building and for whom
  - Optionally runs 4 parallel research agents to map the domain                                                                                    
  - Defines scoped requirements (v1, v2, out-of-scope) with unique REQ-IDs                                                                          
  - Creates a roadmap with phases, goals, and success criteria                                                                                      
                                                                                                                                                    
  Creates:                                                                                                                                          
  .planning/                                                                                                                                        
  ├── PROJECT.md        ← vision, decisions, key context                                                                                            
  ├── REQUIREMENTS.md   ← all requirements with IDs (SUB-01, CRM-02, etc.)                                                                          
  ├── ROADMAP.md        ← phases with goals and success criteria                                                                                    
  ├── STATE.md          ← project memory, updated after every action                                                                                
  └── config.json       ← workflow mode (interactive vs YOLO)                                                                                       
                                                                                                                                                    
  After this: /clear to start fresh, then plan Phase 1.                                                                                             
                                                                                                                                                    
  ---                                                                                                                                               
  Planning a Phase                                                                                                                                  
                                                                                                                                                    
  Optional: Capture your vision first          
                                                                                                                                                    
  /gsd:discuss-phase 1                       
  If you have opinions about how something should look or work, run this before planning. It asks targeted questions and creates CONTEXT.md — a file
   of locked decisions the planner must follow. Skip it if you're happy letting Claude make all design calls.                                       
                                                                                                                                                    
  Create the plan                                                                                                                                   
                                               
  /gsd:plan-phase 1                            
  This is the main planning command. It:                                                                                                            
  1. Researches the domain — checks official docs, package versions, known pitfalls                                                                 
  2. Creates PLAN.md files — concrete tasks with exact file paths, code snippets, and grep-verifiable acceptance criteria                           
  3. Verifies the plan — a checker agent reviews whether the plan actually achieves the phase goal (up to 3 revision rounds)                        
                                                                                                                                                    
  Creates in .planning/phases/01-your-phase/:                                                                                                       
  01-RESEARCH.md      ← what the researcher found                                                                                                   
  01-VALIDATION.md    ← test strategy (Nyquist validation)                                                                                          
  01-PLAN-01-name.md  ← executable plan with tasks                                                                                                  
  01-PLAN-02-name.md  ← second plan (if phase has parallel work)                                                                                    
                                                                                                                                                    
  After this: /clear to start fresh, then execute.                                                                                                  
                                                                                                                                                    
  ---                                                                                                                                               
  Executing a Phase                                                                                                                                 
                                               
  /gsd:execute-phase 1                         
  Runs all plans in the phase. Plans are grouped into waves (wave 1 runs first, wave 2 runs after, etc.). Plans within the same wave run in parallel
   using separate Claude agents.                                                                                                                    
                                                                                                                                                    
  After execution:                                                                                                                                  
  - Creates SUMMARY.md for each plan           
  - Runs verification against the phase goal                                                                                                        
  - Updates STATE.md, ROADMAP.md, and REQUIREMENTS.md
                                                                                                                                                    
  ---                                                                                                                                               
  The Full Workflow (Your Project)             
                                                                                                                                                    
  Your project has 4 phases:                 
                                                                                                                                                    
  Phase 1: Infrastructure          ← subdomain middleware + Neon/Drizzle DB
  Phase 2: Content and CRM         ← photography gallery, pricing, contact capture                                                                  
  Phase 3: Booking and Payments    ← Stripe deposit, CalDAV, confirmation email                                                                     
  Phase 4: GEO and Ecommerce       ← JSON-LD schema, llms.txt, ecommerce landing                                                                    
                                                                                                                                                    
  Each phase follows the same pattern:                                                                                                              
  /clear                                                                                                                                            
  /gsd:plan-phase N      ← plan it (research → plan → verify)
  /clear                                                     
  /gsd:execute-phase N   ← build it                                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                                                    
