  Model Profiles
                
  GSD uses multiple Claude agents. You can control which model each uses:
                                                                                                                                                    
  ┌────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐                                                                    
  │      Profile       │                       Use when                        │                                                                    
  ├────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                                                    
  │ balanced (default) │ Normal work — Opus for planning, Sonnet for execution │
  ├────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                                                    
  │ quality            │ Architecture-heavy phases — Opus everywhere           │                                                                    
  ├────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                                                    
  │ budget             │ High-volume work or when conserving quota             │                                                                    
  ├────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                                                    
  │ inherit            │ Follow whatever model you have set in the session     │
  └────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘                                                                    
                                             
  /gsd:set-profile budget                                                                                                                           
  /gsd:set-profile quality                                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                                                    
  ---                                                                                                                                               
  Workflow Modes                                                                                                                                    
                                               
  Set when you ran /gsd:new-project. Your project is on YOLO mode — Claude auto-approves decisions and doesn't pause for confirmations. Change in
  .planning/config.json:                                                                                                                            
   
  { "mode": "interactive" }   ← pauses at checkpoints for approval                                                                                  
  { "mode": "yolo" }          ← full autonomy, minimal interruptions                                                                                
                                                                                                                                                    
  ---                                                                                                                                               
  What is Ralph-Loop?                                                                                                                               
                                                                                                                                                    
  Ralph-loop is a self-correcting iteration tool. Instead of running a command once and hoping it works, ralph-loop runs the command in a loop —
  each time Claude exits, the same prompt is fed back automatically. Claude sees its previous work in files and git history, and improves on it.    
                                             
  It's built on a Stop hook: when Claude tries to end the session, the hook intercepts the exit and re-injects the original prompt.                 
                                             
  Named after Ralph Wiggum. The philosophy: keep trying until it's actually done.                                                                   
                                             
  ---                                                                                                                                               
  How to Use Ralph-Loop                      
                                               
  Basic usage
                                                                                                                                                    
  /ralph-loop <your task> --completion-promise "DONE" --max-iterations 5
                                                                                                                                                    
  - --completion-promise — the exact phrase Claude must output (inside <promise> tags) to stop the loop. Claude can only output it when it's        
  genuinely true.                                                                                                                                   
  - --max-iterations — safety cap. Always set this. Without it, the loop runs forever.                                                              
                                                                                                                                                    
  Cancel an active loop                                                                                                                             
                                                                                                                                                    
  /cancel-ralph                                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                                                    
  With GSD: execute a phase in a loop                                                                                                               
                                                                                                                                                    
  This is the most powerful combination. Instead of running execute-phase once and hoping it works, run it in a loop so Claude keeps fixing failures
   until the phase is genuinely complete:      
                                                                                                                                                    
  /ralph-loop /gsd:execute-phase 1 --completion-promise "PHASE 1 COMPLETE" --max-iterations 5
                                                                                         
  What happens:                                                                                                                                     
  1. Claude runs /gsd:execute-phase 1                                                                                                               
  2. If tests fail, build breaks, or verification fails — Claude tries to exit                                                                      
  3. The Stop hook blocks exit and feeds the same prompt back                 
  4. Claude sees the failed state in files and git, diagnoses the problem, and tries again                                                          
  5. Repeats until Claude outputs <promise>PHASE 1 COMPLETE</promise> or hits 5 iterations                                                          
                                                                                                                                                    
  Phase-by-phase pattern                                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                                                    
  /clear                                                                                                                                            
  /gsd:plan-phase 1                                                                                                                                 
  /clear                                       
  /ralph-loop /gsd:execute-phase 1 --completion-promise "PHASE 1 COMPLETE" --max-iterations 5
                                                                                                                                                    
  /clear
  /gsd:plan-phase 2                                                                                                                                 
  /clear                                     
  /ralph-loop /gsd:execute-phase 2 --completion-promise "PHASE 2 COMPLETE" --max-iterations 5                                                       
                                                                                                                                                    
  ---                                                                                                                                               
  When to Use ralph-loop vs not                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                                                    
  Use ralph-loop when:                         
  - Executing phases with build steps, tests, or migrations that can fail                                                                           
  - You want to walk away and let Claude handle failures autonomously                                                                               
  - The task has clear, verifiable success criteria (tests pass, build succeeds)                                                                    
                                                                                                                                                    
  Skip ralph-loop when:                                                                                                                             
  - Planning phases (planning doesn't need iteration — do it once, then clear)                                                                      
  - Tasks requiring judgment calls you need to review                                                                                               
  - Debugging (use /gsd:debug instead — it has its own state management)
  - Quick one-off edits (/gsd:quick is faster)                                                                                                      
                                                                                                                                                    
  ---                                                                                                                                               
  Writing Good Completion Promises                                                                                                                  
                                                                                                                                                    
  The completion promise must be something Claude can only honestly claim when done. Bad promises let Claude exit too early.
                                                                                                                                                    
  ┌─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────┐
  │             Bad             │                Good                 │                                                                             
  ├─────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ "DONE" (too vague)          │ "ALL TESTS PASSING"                 │
  ├─────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ "FINISHED"                  │ "PHASE 1 COMPLETE"                  │                                                                             
  ├─────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────┤                                                                             
  │ "COMPLETE" with no criteria │ "BUILD SUCCEEDS AND MIGRATIONS RAN" │                                                                             
  └─────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────┘                                                                             
                                               
  Claude is instructed not to output the promise if it's not true — it won't lie to escape the loop.                                                
                                             
  ---                                                                                                                                               
  Practical Tips                             
                                                                                                                                                    
  Always /clear between major steps. Context windows fill up fast with agent output. Plan-phase and execute-phase are heavy. Fresh context = better
  results.                                                                                                                                          
                                             
  Check progress anytime:                                                                                                                           
  /gsd:progress                              
                                               
  When something breaks mid-phase:
  /gsd:debug "describe what broke"                                                                                                                  
  This creates a persistent debug session that survives /clear. Run /gsd:debug with no args to resume.
                                                                                                                                                    
  Captured a random idea during work:                                                                                                               
  /gsd:note refactor the booking form validation                                                                                                    
  Zero friction, saved instantly. Promote it to a todo later.                                                                                       
                                                                                                                                                    
  Burned through quota mid-phase:                                                                                                                   
  /gsd:set-profile budget                                                                                                                           
  Switches all agents to cheaper models mid-flight. No need to restart.                                                                             
                                                                       
  Stuck and don't know what to run next:                                                                                                            
  /gsd:do <describe what you want in plain English>                                                                                                 
  It routes to the right command automatically.                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                                                    
